WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.067
<v Examiner>Four marks.

2
00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:05.175
<v Examiner>Define family in the context of family-centred care,

3
00:00:05.175 --> 00:00:10.314
<v Examiner>and describe the three principles that make up a partnership with the person and their

4
00:00:10.314 --> 00:00:10.733
<v Examiner>family.

5
00:00:11.183 --> 00:00:14.540
Family is whoever the person identifies as family,

6
00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:17.294
with or without biological or legal ties.

7
00:00:17.294 --> 00:00:22.733
Structures vary: blended families, single parents, shared care, same-sex parents,

8
00:00:22.733 --> 00:00:24.076
and extended whānau.

9
00:00:24.076 --> 00:00:28.105
For some people it includes long-term friends and even pets.

10
00:00:28.105 --> 00:00:32.537
So the first move is always to ask the person who their family is.

11
00:00:32.987 --> 00:00:36.422
The three principles that make up partnership, from Lisa's deck.

12
00:00:36.872 --> 00:00:38.038
One, relationship.

13
00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:42.249
A genuine and mutually respectful relationship between the nurse,

14
00:00:42.249 --> 00:00:43.933
the person and the family.

15
00:00:44.383 --> 00:00:46.609
Two, participation and involvement.

16
00:00:46.609 --> 00:00:49.979
Respecting the autonomy of the person and the family,

17
00:00:49.979 --> 00:00:54.303
and involving them in care and decisions as much as they want to be.

18
00:00:54.753 --> 00:00:56.094
Three, tailoring care.

19
00:00:56.094 --> 00:01:01.089
Care fitted to their needs, strengths, limits and context, not a standard package.

20
00:01:01.539 --> 00:01:06.065
At the core are empowerment and advocacy, which she linked to Te Tiriti.

21
00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:10.905
In practice: involve them, keep communicating, find out what matters to them,

22
00:01:10.905 --> 00:01:12.539
and put services in place.

23
00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:17.379
In the multi-choice, the principle the practice quiz asks for is partnership,

24
00:01:17.379 --> 00:01:20.270
and what nursing now centres on is the client.

25
00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:26.404
Family: whoever the person says is family, with or without biological or legal ties.

26
00:01:26.404 --> 00:01:31.140
Three principles of partnership: relationship, genuine and respectful;

27
00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:37.027
participation and involvement, respecting autonomy; tailoring care to needs, strengths,

28
00:01:37.027 --> 00:01:38.313
limits and context.

29
00:01:38.313 --> 00:01:40.411
Core: empowerment and advocacy.
